A letter is a "letteral", although the reverse is not always true.
"letteral" is the English coined word the designers made up to include
things which are not letters but work like one: {'}, {,}, and {.}. {lerfu}
doesn't mean "letter" or "letteral" interchangably, it always means
"letteral". Just like "truck" is "vehicle", but "vehicle" isn't always
"truck". (car, boat, plane, etc.)


